---
description: Tests and quality rules
globs:
  - "tests/**/*.php"
  - "phpunit.xml*"
  - "phpstan.neon*"
  - "rector.php"
  - ".php-cs-fixer.dist.php"
alwaysApply: false
---

When changing behavior, prefer adding or updating the nearest relevant test
(`tests/Unit/<Namespace>/` mirrors `src/`, container wiring in `tests/Integration/`).

Prefer:
- one focused test
- PHPUnit attributes (`#[DataProvider]`, `#[CoversClass]`, ...), never `@test` / `@dataProvider` docblocks
- `Symfony\Component\Clock\MockClock` for time and an in-memory PSR-3 logger for log assertions
- obvious placeholders such as `REDACTED-TEST` instead of realistic secrets in fixtures
- preserving the existing testing style

Keep PHP line coverage at 100% (`make test-coverage`; CI enforces it). PHPStan stays at level 8 with no ignores (`make phpstan`).

Do not introduce new testing frameworks unless explicitly requested.
Do not rewrite unrelated tests.
